<section class="sec tint">
<div class="wrap two">
<div>
<h2>Where We Go</h2>
<p>We target sharks in the beautiful backcountry of the Florida Keys. There are hundreds of square miles of prime, fishable shark waters. We like water less than 4 or 5 feet deep and very clear. We look for moving water where a flat might be draining into a channel or basins that provide great ambush points. We use Power-poles to hold us stationary and sight cast to them as they cruise up the chum slicks to the boat. More times than not, you actually pick the one you want with so many around the boat. In the shallows sharks naturally feed on Barracuda, Stingrays, schools of Mullet or small fish for food. Most often, customers are amazed at how big a shark will be for only a few feet of water.</p>
</div>
